From 89f81feb8d6f5b10a1d2731b522ff3942f0f811c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] drm/tests: Add tests for the HDMI "Dolby Vision" property

Test the property's names and creation, its default (Off), that a
change of it is a mode change and that setting the same value isn't,
the vendor and AVI infoframes of each value with and without an HDMI_VIC
mode and on a sink without HDMI_Video_present, and that each output the
tunnelled signal doesn't survive (limited range, Automatic range on a
CEA mode, 12 bpc, YUV 4:2:0, a BT.2020 colorspace, HDR output metadata,
an interlaced mode, a DVI sink) is rejected with Dolby Vision and
accepted without it.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_connector_test.c    | 102 +++
 .../drm/tests/drm_hdmi_state_helper_test.c    | 582 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 684 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_connector_test.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_connector_test.c
index 6cfdce96f..49c27795b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_connector_test.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tests/drm_connector_test.c
@@ -1389,6 +1389,63 @@ static struct kunit_suite drm_hdmi_connector_get_broadcast_rgb_name_test_suite =
 	.test_cases = drm_hdmi_connector_get_broadcast_rgb_name_tests,
 };
 
